    "final_cot": "Image description: From the figure it can be seen that Q, R, S, T are on the same upper slanted side, and Q, X, W, V are on the same horizontal bottom side; segments RX, SW, TV have the same pink arrow markings, indicating that they are parallel to each other. The problem gives QR=2, XW=12, QW=15, ST=5. Reasoning: Because Q, X, W are collinear, and X is between Q and W, QX=QW−XW=15−12=3. Since RX ∥ SW, and QX and QW are on the same straight line, QR and QS are on the same straight line, triangle QXR is similar to triangle QWS. Therefore QR/QS=QX/QW=3/15=1/5. Substituting QR=2, get 2/QS=1/5, so QS=10. Also because Q, R, S are collinear, RS=QS−QR=10−2=8.",
